{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 3, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 5098357097177862029, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 642, "mtime": 1791871732.3920498, "sha256": "2003bb278f74f918562b0157674990e77cf6248fcc76b5d3c7b0c7aafcfb622c"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 577, "mtime": 1791871735.8363228, "sha256": "a5d74d0a119db5855ff5ab1eb6c96ed6574ac8dab3a3abfbf07dbd743e2fc13f"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/6/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/6/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test, then running.\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Why it happened:** a float can't hold 2.675 exactly. Python stores it as `2.67499999999999982\u2026`, so `round(x, 2)` rounds it down. On top of that, `round()` rounds exact ties to the nearest even digit, so `round(0.125, 2)` gives `0.12`. That breaks the \"half up\" promise in the function's own docstring.\n\n**Fix (`pricing/money.py`):** turn the float into a `Decimal` using `repr(x)`, which gives the short decimal form people expect (`\"2.675\"`). Then round to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP` and convert back to `float`. The function still returns the same type, so `add_vat` didn't need any changes. Negative values round half away from zero, so `-2.675` becomes `-2.68`.\n\n**Checks:** pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the cases directly with `python3`. All of these came back correct: `2.675\u21922.68`, `1.005\u21921.01`, `0.125\u21920.13`, `2.665\u21922.67`, `2.674\u21922.67`, `-2.675\u2192-2.68`, `3\u21923.0`. `add_vat(10.0)` gives `12.0`, and the existing `split(10.00, 3)` result is unchanged. I added the same cases as tests in `tests/test_round_money.py`, but they haven't been run under pytest.\n\n**One limitation:** `add_vat` multiplies floats before rounding, and that multiplication can introduce its own tiny error before `round_money` sees the value. If a price \u00d7 VAT result lands exactly on a half cent, it could still round the wrong way. Fixing that properly means doing the money arithmetic in `Decimal` throughout. I didn't change that because you only asked about `round_money`.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 10, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 271501, "requests_cache_write": 15457, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1784132, "requests_count": 10, "req